Fixed! Here's what was causing those errors:
1. Site Builder - "No modules found" Error (site-builder.js:512)
Problem: The /api/page/save endpoint was rejecting pages that had no existing [data-module] elements in the HTML. This meant you couldn't:

Add the first module to a new page
Save a page after removing all modules
Use the site builder on pages without pre-existing modules
Fix (server.js:3174):

Changed logic to find a suitable container when no modules exist
Looks for .action-module, <main>, or <body> as fallback containers
Only errors if you try to save with an empty modules array
Now properly handles both new and existing module scenarios
2. CSS Editor - "Cannot read properties of undefined" Error (css-editor.html:514, 792)
Problem: Property name mismatch between the API and the frontend:

Server sent: { cssContent: "..." }
Frontend expected: { css: "..." }
This caused data.css to be undefined, leading to the error when calling .match()
Fix:

server.js:3696 - Changed /api/css/load response from cssContent → css
server.js:3713 - Changed /api/css/save request param from cssContent → css
server.js:3730 - Updated the variable usage to match
3. Module Loader - "Found 0 modules" (module-loader.js:122)
This was a symptom of issue #1 - when the page save failed, no modules were being written to the HTML, so the module-loader couldn't find any [data-module] elements to load.

